          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ദയയുള്ള — dayayuḷḷa — \"kind-hearted; kind\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ദയയുള്ള ഒരു സ്ത്രീ എനിക്ക് വഴി പറഞ്ഞുതന്നു. dayayuḷḷa oru strī enikkŭ vaḻi paṟaññutannu. A kind woman told me the way."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ദയ, kindness, + ഉള്ള, having. ദയവായി, please, holds the same noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ദയയുള്ള (dayayuḷḷa) is built from ദയ, from Sanskrit dayā, \"sympathy, compassion\" (CDIAL 6185), and the native ending -ഉള്ള, \"having\" (DEDR 697)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
